comments:
No +1's please. This just creates unnecessary noise for everyone.

@keszybz already acknowledged the issue at https://www.spinics.net/lists/fedora-devel/msg300564.html

What it needs now is a fix/PR, no further me-toos.

> > I believe it's because of this commit [cdf3706](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/commit/cdf370626f08ed509a5dde9d5618eed29d625032)
> 
> I don't think. When disabled, the messages remain.

Then I believe 90b1ec0 caused this since reverting both cdf3706 and the following part of 90b1ec0 removes messages at least for suspend.
```diff
diff --git a/src/login/logind-utmp.c b/src/login/logind-utmp.c
index 5533836473..d2b2f8b193 100644
--- a/src/login/logind-utmp.c
+++ b/src/login/logind-utmp.c
@@ -135,11 +135,11 @@ int manager_setup_wall_message_timer(Manager *m) {
                 return 0;
         }
 
-        if (elapse < n)
+        if (elapse > 0 && elapse < n)
                 return 0;
 
         /* Warn immediately if less than 15 minutes are left */
-        if (elapse - n < 15 * USEC_PER_MINUTE) {
+        if (elapse == 0 || elapse - n < 15 * USEC_PER_MINUTE) {
                 r = warn_wall(m, n);
                 if (r == 0)
                         return 0;
```
